        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): honor timeoutSeconds for dynamic tool calls when timeoutMs is absent",
        "body": "Fixes #98864.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nCodex dynamic tool calls can specify `timeoutSeconds` while omitting `timeoutMs`. `resolveDynamicToolCallTimeoutMs` previously only read `timeoutMs`, so a tool configured with a seconds-only timeout fell back to the default 90s deadline instead of honoring the caller's intent. The side-question path (`resolveSideDynamicToolCallTimeoutMs`) had the same gap. Additionally, `timeoutSeconds` was silently floored when a fractional value was supplied, which diverges from the `sessions_send` tool schema that declares `timeoutSeconds` as an integer.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- `readDynamicToolCallTimeoutMs` now falls back to `readTimeoutSecondsAsMs(value.timeoutSeconds)` when `timeoutMs` is absent or invalid.\n- `readSideDynamicToolCallTimeoutMs` mirrors the main path and also falls back to `readSideTimeoutSecondsAsMs(value.timeoutSeconds)`.\n- Both `readTimeoutSecondsAsMs` and `readSideTimeoutSecondsAsMs` now require `Number.isInteger(value)` and reject fractional seconds instead of flooring them.\n- `timeoutMs` still takes precedence when both are present.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDynamic tools that pass `timeoutSeconds` (e.g. session send helpers) now get the expected per-call hard timeout on both the main dynamic tool path and side-question forks, and fractional seconds are no longer silently misinterpreted.\n\n## Evidence\n\nUnit tests:\n\n```bash\npnpm test extensions/codex/src/app-server/dynamic-tool-execution.test.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/side-question.test.ts\n```\n\n```\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\n     Tests  60 passed (60)\n```\n\nReal behavior proof (exercises the actual runtime handlers with a tool that intentionally sleeps past the deadline):\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/codex-dynamic-tool-timeout-seconds.mts\n```\n\n```\n=== Proof: Codex dynamic tool timeoutSeconds support ===\n\nresolver/main: timeoutSeconds only: expected 30000ms, got 30000ms PASS\nresolver/main: timeoutMs takes precedence: expected 5000ms, got 5000ms PASS\nresolver/main: non-positive timeoutSeconds falls back to default: expected 90000ms, got 90000ms PASS\nresolver/main: fractional timeoutSeconds falls back to default: expected 90000ms, got 90000ms PASS\nresolver/side: timeoutSeconds only: expected 45000ms, got 45000ms PASS\nresolver/side: timeoutMs takes precedence: expected 5000ms, got 5000ms PASS\nresolver/side: fractional timeoutSeconds falls back to default: expected 90000ms, got 90000ms PASS\nruntime/main: timeoutSeconds is enforced by handleDynamicToolCallWithTimeout: PASS\nruntime/main: timeoutMs still takes precedence over timeoutSeconds: PASS\nruntime/side: timeoutSeconds is enforced by handleSideDynamicToolCallWithTimeout: PASS\nruntime/side: timeoutMs still takes precedence over timeoutSeconds: PASS\n\nAll cases passed.\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/codex-dynamic-tool-timeout-seconds",
